  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Richards is a 64-year-old woman who returns for her yearly preventive visit, eight weeks after her six-month bone health review. She has low bone mass with a high 10-year fracture risk and had her first yearly zoledronic acid infusion in May. She takes vitamin D3 1971 units a day and gets about 1200 mg of calcium a day from food. She keeps up the home balance program three times a week, walks most days, and lifts weights twice a week. She has had no falls. She has had no alcohol and remains in sustained remission. She completed the health risk assessment before the visit and has no new concerns. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No falls, fractures, emergency visits, or hospital stays this year</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Vitamin D3 1971 units daily; zoledronic acid once a year (next dose in May); no over-the-counter sleep aids or sedatives</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Low bone mass with high fracture risk, on treatment; alcohol use disorder in sustained remission; history of falls, none this year</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent; travels most weeks for work</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Very good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Busy with speaking and advisory work; close family and friends; no loneliness; stress manageable</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Former smoker; no tobacco or vaping for more than fifteen years</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>No alcohol (AUDIT-C 0); no other drug use; recovery steady</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks 30 minutes most days, weight training twice a week, balance routine three times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>About 1200 mg of calcium a day from food; protein at each meal; two cups of coffee a day</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours a night; some short nights when traveling</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Independent, including driving, finances, and medicines</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Stair rails on both sides, night lights, no loose rugs; smoke detectors working; seat belt always</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>No falls this year; less fear of falling since the balance program</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Reading glasses; eye examination this year; no hearing difficulty</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>No concerns</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

