    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression, alcohol, and fall-risk screens are negative. 10-year atherosclerotic cardiovascular risk about 5 percent (total cholesterol 204, HDL 62, systolic 122, nonsmoker, no diabetes), below the threshold for a statin. [S]<list><item>Influenza and PCV20 vaccines today.</item><item>COVID-19 vaccine at her pharmacy this month.</item><item>Next mammogram in about ten months.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Low bone mass with high fracture risk, on zoledronic acid (M85.89)</content>. First yearly dose given in May; CTX fell 66 percent by August. Height unchanged, no falls or fractures, no jaw or thigh symptoms. [S]<list><item>Continue vitamin D3 1971 units daily and calcium from food.</item><item>Second dose in May after calcium, creatinine, and 25-hydroxyvitamin D.</item><item>DXA two years after starting.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder in sustained remission (F10.21)</content>. No alcohol; AUDIT-C 0. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline is saved in her phone. [S]<list><item>Continue the recovery check at each visit.</item><item>No sedating medicines.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">History of falls (Z91.81)</content>. No falls this year; balance and gait improved since the exercise program. [S]<list><item>Continue the home balance program three times a week.</item><item>Yearly fall-risk screen and eye examination.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; recommended once for all adults 50 and older; no further dose needed</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; she will get it at her pharmacy this month</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two-dose series completed three years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap seven years ago; next due in about three years</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended at 50 to 74 only with a risk condition; she has none</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Screening mammogram every two years from 40 to 74; last normal 14 months ago; next in about ten months</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>HPV test negative three years ago with earlier normal results; screening can stop after 65 with adequate negative results</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Colonoscopy normal six years ago; next in four years</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Former heavy smoker, but she quit more than 15 years ago, so she does not meet the criteria</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol screening and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>LDL 118 mg/dL; 10-year risk about 5 percent; no statin; recheck in five years or if risk changes</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended at 35 to 70 with overweight or obesity; BMI 24.5</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>122/74 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C and HIV screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>One-time screening for both done in the past, negative</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0; PHQ-9 2 in February</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 0; sustained remission</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Former smoker; no use</td></tr><tr><td>Osteoporosis screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Already diagnosed and on treatment; follow-up DXA two years after starting</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; Timed Up and Go 9 seconds; home balance program continues</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity and diet counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Weight-bearing, strength, and balance exercise; calcium from food</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Done this year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 1997-1998 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20, single dose [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, osteoporosis monograph (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: COVID-19 vaccine at her pharmacy. Mammogram in about ten months. Second zoledronic acid dose in May with pre-infusion tests. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
